<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parakramabahu I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1123–1186</span> · Also known as Parakramabahu the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Parakramabahu I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> from 1153 to 1186, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polonnaruwa">Polonnaruwa</a>. After a long civil war he reunited the island, reformed and unified the Buddhist sangha, and built great irrigation works, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parakrama-samudra">Parakrama Samudra</a>, and monuments such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gal-vihara">Gal Vihara</a>. He also sent military expeditions to southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>. He is regarded as one of the greatest Sinhalese kings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/parakramabahu-i.jpg" alt="Parakramabahu I" width="320" height="509" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Graham Racher from London, UK · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Relief_of_Parakramabahu_in_Polonnaruwa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
